              "text": "плита (plitá) — Old Russian плита (plitá), \"a stone slab, a brick\". Vasmer thinks it most likely a cousin of Greek plínthos, \"brick\"; the common view takes it as a loan from that Greek word. A плита (plitá) is the slab you cook on."
